WEBVTT

NOTE
Landscape prototype walkthrough. These captions are also burned into the video
frame; this track exists for accessibility tooling, text extraction and reuse.

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Landscape answers one question: who else is already doing what you are planning to do?

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.500
You describe your idea in the box, in your own words. That is the only thing you have to do.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.000
Here the idea is an app that helps small farms sell straight to local restaurants.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.500
First it works out what to call this line of business, then goes looking for companies already in it.

5
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.500
It reads each company own website. One site does not allow automated reading, so it is skipped, and the report will say so.

6
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.500
It found three companies you may never have heard of. That is the point: you do not have to know the names in advance.

7
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.500
Prices come first. They are taken straight from each company own price page, so the figures are exactly what they published.

8
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.500
One company does not publish a price at all, so the report says that instead of guessing.

9
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.500
A price found on somebody blog, which we could not confirm on the company own site, is kept out of the table.

10
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:41.500
Then the written part appears, a few words at a time.

11
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:46.500
The table of what each one does is careful. A question mark means we looked and found nothing said either way.

12
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.500
And a triangle means a rival claimed it, not the company itself.

13
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.500
When a company does not say what it has changed, the report says exactly that, and lists everywhere it looked.

14
00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:01.500
Customer reviews are read for what people wish the product did. Six people wanted a different price list for each restaurant. That is a gap you could build into.

15
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:07.500
Every fact links back to where it came from. Click one and you see the page, the exact sentence, and when it was read.

16
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:16.500
Once the report is ready you can ask questions about it. Answers come back quickly, because the pages have already been read.

17
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:22.500
Ask something the pages do not cover, and it tells you, instead of making an answer up.

18
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.500
Without signing up you get one report a day. The report itself is complete: nothing hidden, nothing stamped across it.

19
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.500
A free account raises that to one report an hour.

20
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.500
A dollar a month gives you five an hour and as many questions as you like. The report is the same either way.

21
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:41.500
If a competitor changes their prices, you get an email. The subject line tells you what changed.

22
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:46.500
And you can see the before and after side by side, both dated, so you can check it yourself.

23
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:52.500
There is a public help area anyone can read. The channels for sign-up and log-in trouble take messages from anyone, because a person who cannot log in cannot be asked to log in first.

24
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.500
Behind the scenes, the owner can see how busy the service is and change any of the limits without touching code.

25
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:01.500
Change a number and it takes effect straight away.

26
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:06.500
That is the whole of it. There are two other ways to start, if you already know something about the market.

27
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:10.500
You can name the competitors yourself, if you already know who they are.

28
00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.500
You can paste the address of a company website, and it will work out the rest.

29
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:19.500
Or put them in the same sentence as your idea. Any of the three work on their own, or together.

30
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:25.500
Facts you can check. Gaps it owns up to. And one thing to type to get started.
